:"openclaw-extra"},"disableModelInvocation":false,"available":true},{"id":"ui-ux-pro-max","name":"ui-ux-pro-max","description":"UI/UX design intelligence and implementation guidance for building polished interfaces. Use when the user asks for UI design, UX flows, information architecture, visual style direction, design systems/tokens, component specs, copy/microcopy, accessibility, or to generate/critique/refine frontend UI (HTML/CSS/JS, React, Next.js, Vue, Svelte, Tailwind). Includes workflows for (1) generating new UI layouts and styling, (2) improving existing UI/UX, (3) producing design-system tokens and component guidelines, and (4) turning UX recommendations into concrete code changes.","filePath":"$OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/workspace/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md","baseDir":"$OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/workspace/skills/ui-ux-pro-max","source":"openclaw-workspace","sourceInfo":{"baseDir":"$OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/workspace/skills/ui-ux-pro-max","origin":"top-level","path":"$OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/workspace/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md","scope":"project","source":"openclaw-workspace"},"disableModelInvocation":false,"available":true},{"id":"vitest-testing","name":"vitest-testing","description":"Vitest testing framework patterns and best practices. Use when writing unit tests, integration tests, configuring vitest.config, mocking with vi.mock/vi.fn, using snapshots, or setting up test coverage. Triggers on describe, it, expect, vi.mock, vi.fn, beforeEach, afterEach, vitest.","filePath":"$OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/workspace/skills/vitest-testing/SKILL.md","baseDir":"$OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/workspace/skills/vitest-testing","source":"openclaw-workspace","sourceInfo":{"baseDir":"$OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/workspace/skills/vitest-testing","origin":"top-level","path":"$OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/workspace/skills/vitest-testing/SKILL.md","scope":"project","source":"openclaw-workspace"},"disableModelInvocation":false,"available":true},{"id":"weather","name":"weather","description":"Current weather and forecasts with w